        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ci.blooming-grove.tx.us/our-history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When a postal station opened in 1871, the community chose the name Blooming Grove.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ci.blooming-grove.tx.us/our-history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1888 a cotton‑belt railroad branch opened, prompting Gradyville to shift one mile northeast and become Blooming Grove.",
